    "notes": [
      "Storybook alchemy, not a chemistry or survival instruction manual. A recipe denotes a recognisable craft relationship, not a physically complete bill of materials.",
      "First design pass. Recipe count is not evidence of game length or fun. Exact required closure and playtester reports are separate evidence.",
      "No choose-N goals, invisible benches, automatic terminal hiding, inventory scarcity or forced timer.",
      "Uses v3 current-scene packing: only the existing prerequisite frontier is brought along; things left behind remain tangible at prior places.",
      "v4 adds concrete material/function descriptions, names the wheeled undercarriage Wheelset, fixes hinge and hammerstone relationships, and folds the one-creation map synthesis into the night-navigation chapter. No quota recipes added.",
      "v5 responds to the full-v4 stop: natural alternate routes retain canonical outputs; fitting the house window now satisfies the actual shelter goal; mill and baker acknowledge prior flour and offer a concrete next reward. No new item or quota recipe added.",
      "v6 observation candidate: the microscope now reveals an observed pond-world; natural sample, specimen and wind-note alternatives preserve their old routes. Guests arrive after scene 21, share the kitchen meal at 24, and stay present through the later craft exchanges and journeys home. No new mechanic, scarcity, timer, choice quota, hidden item retirement or artificial prerequisite. Author-aware validation is not a fresh player retest.",
      "Opening-wheel research candidate: first chapter makes Stone and Brick, preserving Stone as chapter-two grinding equipment. Bowl is formed from Clay and the earlier Wheel when it first becomes useful for the bakery basket. No original raw inputs, other recipe pairs, runtime rules or later objectives change. Not promoted or human-tested.",
      "House-components v1: the same House has two required unlabelled component slots (Window and Sleeping mat), with an optional Hearth from the previously unused Stone + Fire pair. The Window supply remains for Tower, Greenhouse and Curtain; the Sleeping mat and Hearth have no outside future use and are incorporated at installation. No global engine, UI, old route, old save identity or first-ten canonical recipe change. Logical validation is not human or browser playtest evidence.",
      "House-and-craft v1: clay jars remain jars after glazing/firing; a distinct blown-glass bottle offers an alternate portable-cider output with shared capability. The optional Hourglass uses clear glass, not opaque ceramic. A stone may chip exposed ore directly; Stone hammer is the familiar name for the unchanged handheld cobble. Patterned cloth is woven from dyed thread, not rewoven finished cloth. Iron is shaped into Nails at the stocked Forge, with heat and smithing tools explicit. The canonical route length, first ten, and House slots remain intact. Firing, glassblowing, smithing and closures are explicit craft compression, not manufacturing or safety instructions.",
      "Opt-in persistent-location successor: chapter beats do not grant stock, import objects, or rearrange the board. Fixed 390×844-reference panels retain all surviving objects; current density acceptance is recorded separately.",
      "Retains the original map, ceramic-float and tower recipe families. Their separately recorded forward-naturalness concerns remain unresolved; this presentation overlay does not claim to fix them.",
      "29 October human playtest: restore the pre-consolidation opening cadence as four genuine river-valley viewpoints. Each arrival uses state-sensitive current-scene carry; earlier food, house and material experiments remain tangible in their earlier scrollback panels. Canonical entries are 4/5/6/6 things; canonical peaks are 7/13/15/14, not a claimed strict ten-object cap. Later merged locations are unchanged pending separate measured restoration.",
      "Whole-journey small-scene continuation: restore state-sensitive chapter-sized carry only at a genuine neighbouring worksite/viewpoint or an explicitly later cleared service of a real setting. Previous panels and their surviving creations remain accessible. No new item is granted after the opening, no recipe is changed, no terminal is hidden, and no static future-visit union is used. Shared artwork is used only for a later service of the same setting; new close views and rooms use their own assets.",
      "Separate authenticity review candidate: a player-built weighted press, visible oilseeds and oil-wick torch; distinguish formed clay from the already-existing fired glazed bowl; use clear glass and honest relative rain levels. Four opening primitives, every location and stock batch stay unchanged. No checklist, calibration or new delivery.",
      "Independent-review successor: remove the Bell and Dinner bell wrappers and their terminal goal rather than invent an unfired-clay metalworking mould. The keeper calls departures from the timetable. Formed bowl now has only its early basket/jar-form and kiln-firing consumers; relative-rain record language is consistent. No new recipe, tool, location, stock or processing chore.",
      "Unregistered journey-cleanup review candidate: remove the three compulsory maps and their navigation/atlas wrappers; finish on useful bridge/cart, dock/sailboat, lighthouse/buoy, actual star observation and the existing gathering lantern. Use Clock + Paper for an explicitly printed hourly return-boat timetable. A wooden chest already stores tools, so remove its hinge promotion and retain hinge for the tripod. No new inventory, stock, location, tool or replacement paperwork. Canonical paper preparation occurs at its first useful visit. Keep hinge preparation at the forge workshop, before its final chest goal; later visit carry should leave that future component here until it is relevant. The inherited recipe remains unrestricted by place; no claim is made that headland forging is physically complete. Arrival/peak and alternative preparation-order measurements are required before release. All predecessors and prior authenticity grades remain unchanged.",
      "Unregistered waterworks review successor: challenge the generic pump finding against ordinary assembly first. A smooth wheel plus open wooden conduit does not visibly choose a lifting principle, so consolidate Pump and Water pump into one noria-style Waterwheel with jars using the existing fired ceramic supply. Keep the reservoir, delivery channel and irrigated-garden payoff; no premade equipment, extra stock, valve/fastener recipes, new place or unrelated Stone hammer/Telescope edits. Prior findings and versions remain immutable. Physical performance, browser pixels and human enjoyment require separate evidence.",
      "Basket/continuity successor: weave plant fiber with existing rope, without a clay-bowl mold or a new tool. The packed-bread picnic remains unchanged. Form the bowl at its first remaining jar use. An automatically skipped-if-prepared quarry return moves the existing charcoal action before landing work: the brick kiln remains resident and only real portable supplies travel. No new recipes, ingredients, stock, artwork or hidden storage. Garden continuity remains separately reviewed. Logical evidence is not native/browser or human-comprehension evidence."
    ],
