      },
      {
        "id": "plain-divinity-not-sensory-proof",
        "item": "not-sensory-proof",
        "when": "created",
        "title": "This explains Aquinas’s claim; tasting the bread does not prove it",
        "text": "Aquinas says the bread becomes Christ’s body while its taste remains. Tasting it therefore cannot prove the change he claims. His account rests on faith in divine authority, not a change detected by the senses.",
