      "v4 responds to the frozen source-blind Refuge/Night sessions: visible matched fictional thermal readings; comparison is an intermediate evidential goal, not a reagent that manufactures a cutting pattern.",
      "A single earned machine-to-existing-bench installation closes the legal tow-old-alias Workshop gap without runtime changes. Required axle and bracket operations use that fitted earlier bench.",
      "Original v3 and its negative/fresh sessions remain immutable. Source-blind action harness must resolve drop gestures with the same dropAction as the browser.",
      "Opt-in persistent-location successor: chapter beats do not grant stock, import objects, or rearrange the board. Fixed 390×844-reference panels retain all surviving objects; current density acceptance is recorded separately.",
      "The two genuine within-chapter journeys are earned by either repaired/towed crawler recovery and by the actual ascent creation. The orbital destination is a hotspot, not a surface inventory grant. Loose gravel is collected with the existing scoop. Other recipe families and objective metadata are retained.",
      "The unpublished location successor removes the scale-card and rack-mounting processing stages. Photograph the actual ice core, compare the existing gravel and ripple photographs directly, and preserve the evidence without claiming calibrated dimensions or life. All historical worlds remain unchanged.",
      "29 October field-scene density successor: prior source groups return at genuine distinct working areas, including separate nursery, thermal, comparison, packing, oxygen, cabin and launch workstations. The restored cadence retains current streamlined core observation, visibly collected gravel and earned recovery/orbital travel. No new item, recipe or goal; no travel deletion. The rescue travel carry now concerns only the recovery/refuge leg, not three later camp chapters.",
      "OPTIONAL isolated fiction, not current canon. The late packing-light reveal was rejected. Discovery occurs during laboratory investigation and uses the existing creation milestone. The creature is the original ice core, with its one sealed tube continuously transported and preserved into the return vehicle. No microbial proof, biological-safety claim or real Mars creature is implied.",
      "Separate authenticity candidate: remove the unrelated ice-photo gate from the basin observation while retaining that photograph and its return-archive use. Mounted-lamp identity repair is deliberately deferred pending a complete two-use state design.",
      "29 October playtest: Dirty water filters into Water directly. Remove the empty-canister/fill wrapper; water serves both seed preparation orders and the existing later pump-loop priming use. Wet seeds are an optional state of the original seeds, not another stock item or plant. Tie downs and insulating blanket can be fitted in either order, preserving the same vestibule and fitted pieces. No runtime, location or artwork change.",
